      "beats": [
        {
          "zone": "notice",
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Mimi notices lights and a fan in an empty meeting area. How can limited resources be used while protecting service? Understand before changing.",
          "start_ms": 0,
          "end_ms": 11520
        },
        {
          "zone": "responsibility",
          "index": 1,
          "text": "She asks about the closing rule and who is responsible. Confirm the right contact at the BHS. A colleague agreeing does not automatically authorize a change.",
          "start_ms": 11820,
          "end_ms": 23340
        },
        {
          "zone": "facts",
          "index": 2,
          "text": "She saw the lights and fan on, with no one there when she checked. The next schedule is unknown. No blame, patient data or invented savings.",
          "start_ms": 23640,
          "end_ms": 33080
        },
        {
          "zone": "service",
          "index": 3,
          "text": "Do not independently reduce supplies. Check service needs and the safety process. No clinical rationing, reuse or electrical repairs beyond the role.",
          "start_ms": 33380,
          "end_ms": 45420
        },
        {
          "zone": "coordinate",
          "index": 4,
          "text": "Mimi shares the observation with the confirmed responsible person. What are the schedule and closing rule? First agreement: review the schedule and checklist, without an immediate change.",
          "start_ms": 45720,
          "end_ms": 58840
        },
        {
          "zone": "summary",
          "index": 5,
          "text": "Practice: describe the concern, check the rule and responsibility, and coordinate before acting. Protect service. Skill is observed separately; online completion alone is insufficient.",
          "start_ms": 59140,
          "end_ms": 74100
        }
      ],
